# tools/ales_crop_witness.rish — crop: keep the named span and drop the rest, the exact complement of ALES2's cut (ALES111).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES111.
# Design read: active-designing/20260815-011317_fill-ales111-lotus-crop.md
# Stands on: lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, its buf/len/samples, the EditError reused whole, and the cut imported by the selftest to prove the complement law),
# lotus/meter.rye (ALES13 — the peak/RMS meter, used only to prove that dropping samples never raises the peak). ALES2's cut REMOVES the named span and keeps everything around
# it (the clip SHRINKS by the span); crop KEEPS the named span and removes everything else (the clip becomes the span) — the Trim to Selection / Crop button every editor ships
# (circle the one phrase worth keeping, drop the rest). Naming it beside cut completes the pair: remove the span, or keep only it.
#
# lotus/crop.rye slides the kept span [start, start+count) to the front in one bounded forward pass and sets the length to count, refusing BadRange when the span falls outside
# the current samples before any write — no second buffer. The crux is four laws. THE CROP LAW: the clip becomes original[start .. start+count) byte for byte, the length exactly
# count. THE COMPLEMENT LAW: crop keeps what cut removes and removes what cut keeps, the crop spliced back into the cut reconstructing the source. THE SUBSET / PEAK LAW: crop
# only drops, so the peak (re-measured through ALES13) is non-increasing. THE DEGENERATE / REFUSAL LAW: crop(0, len) the identity, crop(start, 0) empty, the empty clip its own
# crop, a span past the samples BadRange.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_crop_witness.rish

say "ales-crop: Language EN — crop keeps the count samples starting at start and drops every sample before and after, so the clip becomes exactly that span, its length exactly count. It is the exact complement of ALES2's cut: cut removes the named span and keeps everything around it, crop keeps the named span and removes everything else. This is the Trim to Selection / Crop button every editor ships — circle the one phrase worth keeping, drop the rest. It reseats an existing span and shortens the length, inventing no sample and changing no value."
say "ales-crop: Style Radiant — the rule is stated positively: slide the kept span [start, start+count) to the front in one bounded forward pass, then set the length to count, refusing BadRange when the span falls outside the samples before any write, no second buffer. It names the remove-vs-keep-only distinction beside cut. The crux stands out as four laws: the crop law (the clip becomes original[start .. start+count) byte for byte, the length exactly count), the complement law (crop keeps what cut removes and removes what cut keeps, the crop spliced back into the cut reconstructing the source), the subset / peak law (crop only drops, so the peak is non-increasing — cropping away the loudest sample strictly lowers it, cropping a span that holds it holds it), and the degenerate / refusal law (crop(0, len) the identity, crop(start, 0) the empty clip, a span past the samples BadRange)."
say "ales-crop: Lens TAME — one mono clip of i16 PCM cropped in place to a bounded span, no allocation and no second buffer; the span is refused by name before any write (BadRange when start or count falls outside the samples, checked without underflow — count against the remainder), reusing ALES2's EditError whole and inventing none of its own; the forward copy dest index is always at or behind its src index (start >= 0), so no live sample is overwritten before it is read; the complement is proven against ALES2's own cut and splice, and the non-increasing peak against ALES13's read-only meter; it invents no sample, changes no value, and reads no byte past len; siloed to lotus/, no real sample rate, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/crop"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/crop.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-crop: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/crop.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-crop: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-crop: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-crop' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-crop: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-crop line"
